WEBVTT

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.000
Hello.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.780
I'm truly glad you could join me today.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.840
You ready to do a fantastic little painting?

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:34.660
Good.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.860
Tell you what, let me show you what I've done up here.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.660
I've got my standard old 18 by 24 inch canvas,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.360
but you use any size canvas you want for your painting,

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.280
and I've covered it with a thin, even coat

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.850
of the liquid white, so it's all ready to go.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.410
Tell you what, let's have them run all the colors

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:51.370
across the screen that you need to paint along with me.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.010
And they'll come across, as usual,

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.610
in the same order as I have them on my palette,

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:57.980
starting with a titanium white and working around.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.000
And while they're doing that, shoot,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.940
Let's go up here and get started.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.710
Then we'll start with just a small amount.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.790
I'll tell you what, let's start with a little tiny,

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.230
tiny touch of the bright red.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.810
And you need very little of this color.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.930
It's quite strong.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:16.160
There we go, just tap a little into the bristles.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.800
Now then, I thought today we'd do just a warm,

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.780
happy little painting.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.160
It's such a super day.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.080
So let's just take and make little criss-cross strokes.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.000
And that's just a little.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.980
lay in, there we go, just a little bit of pink in the sky.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.530
Little touch of pink.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.120
Now be very careful, this red is so strong,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.900
it'll look like there's a fire in the sky.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.080
So use a very small amount, very small amount.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.820
You can always add more,

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:51.540
but it's a sign of a gun to try to take it out.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:55.120
You can if you have to, but it's hard to do.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.240
There we go.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.000
And this is continually blending with the liquid white

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.740
and it gets lighter and lighter.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:09.590
Allow the liquid white to work for you, okay?

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.090
As I say, you can make it any degree of brightness

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.750
that you want.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:17.190
Now then, without even cleaning the brush,

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.610
I'm gonna go right into a small amount of the Phthalo Blue

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.470
and just tap a little bit of that into the bristles.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:25.130
Just a small amount.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.910
Once again, these colors are very strong.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.860
It takes very little paint, okay?

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.700
Now then, still using a little criss-cross strokes,

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:40.090
let's just begin laying in some light blue areas

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.110
around this pink.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:43.840
Just sort of let your imagination go here

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.880
and you decide where you want it to be.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.420
Just like so, just let it blend together.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.020
But don't cover up your pink.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.510
The blue is many, many times stronger than the pink.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.650
It'll just eat it up and leave you

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.000
with a totally blue sky, okay?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.160
over in here we want a little bit, like so.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.220
Let's see how you can take this,

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.760
let's do it right here, you can take this blue

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.420
and go right over the pink, and away it goes.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:20.010
It'll just go away and leave you, there.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.190
Okay, maybe you wanna put the indication here and there

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:24.050
of just a happy little cloud that floats out here.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.370
All you have to do is take some of this and just tap it,

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:29.420
and you can bring all kinds of little projections

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.000
out into yourself.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.640
wherever you want 'em, wherever.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.160
Tell you what, maybe over in here.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.220
Shoot, let's have some bigger ones over in here.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:41.610
Sort of let 'em just work off the brush.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.480
Just have fun with it, enjoy.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.570
I say over and over again, and I'm very sincere about it,

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.280
painting should make you happy.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:54.540
It should just make your heart full of joy.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.010
Now very lightly, very lightly here,

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.000
all we have to do is just blend all this.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.540
like this, and you can bring all this together.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:09.500
Now then, while we have that blue on the brush,

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:12.420
you know me and my water, I'm crazy about water.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.630
So let's take a little of the blue,

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:17.990
just tap a little on there, and let's go right down here.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:21.500
I don't know exactly where we're gonna have water yet,

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.220
but let's just lay some on.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:30.000
Anything that we don't want, we'll just cover up, because this

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.240
and we can create any kind of illusion that we want.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:37.130
Don't worry about it, don't worry about it.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.680
We don't make mistakes, we have happy accidents.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.960
And it's very good to keep that in mind.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.520
It'll get you over worrying about,

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:52.600
maybe I've done something wrong, or just enjoy it.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.880
Okay, we'll wash our brush with odorless thinner.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:05:00.000
Shake off the excess, and just

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.540
Beat the devil out of it.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:05.910
I'm going back into a little touch of the bright red.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:09.550
And maybe right in here, in this area I left light,

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:13.200
I'll put a little tiny amount of the red.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.310
Takes very little color.

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:16.630
And we'll let a little of that sky color

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.900
just reflect right down in here.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.820
And then very lightly, three hairs and some air,

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.430
we can blend all this together.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.560
And in the sky, you can blend this

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.090
where the blue and the pink come together.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.000
Just blend it.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.160
until you can't tell where one color stops

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:34.920
and the next color starts.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:40.020
Just using little criss-cross strokes.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.260
Just very soft.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:43.460
And when you're doing this at home,

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.650
stand back and take a look-see.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:46.950
Sometimes when you're right up close,

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:50.230
it's hard to tell exactly what something looks like.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.490
Stand back and look at it.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.460
Move back maybe five, six feet.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:59.120
There we go.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:05:59.960
Okay.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:03.400
And that quick, we have a nice little sky.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.940
It's a very simple sky and you can do it

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.220
with absolutely no problem.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.520
Let's make a little mountain today.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.960
And today, let's make a mountain that looks like

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.060
it's far, far off in the distance.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:17.250
And one of the ways you do that is by size.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.730
So I'm gonna take some black, midnight black,

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:22.670
some Van Dyke brown,

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.800
and we'll put a little alizarin crimson into it.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.630
Black, brown, and a little crimson.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.000
Pull that out as flat as you can get it.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.500
and really get strong with it.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.860
Then take your knife and just cut across.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.120
That's all there is to it.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.480
And you get that little roll of paint

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.540
right out of the edge of the knife.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.820
Now then, you have to make your first major decision.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.680
Where does your mountain live?

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.280
Once again, we want to keep these mountains quite small.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.810
So let's go right up in here and say

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:51.120
maybe there's a little beak that lives there.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:55.730
Comes right on up, see, wherever you want it here.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:58.340
And you're using a lot of pressure.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.000
Get tough with it.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.700
You got all your frustrations and your hostilities.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:12.820
Really push this right into the fabric.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.220
You can scrape off all the excess paint.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:20.250
The value, or the color, is gonna be in the material.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.910
You can't get it off now if you want it off.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:24.850
It's the sun, we're gonna try to get that off.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:29.670
Okay, now with our big brush, grab it and just firmly pull it.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:31.960
Just pull it.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:34.460
Because it's wet underneath, the paint will move.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:35.860
It'll slide.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:39.440
See there?

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.440
This is also a good way to lay out your highlights

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.740
and shadows without being committed.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:45.580
You can sort of see here where your brush strokes go.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:49.550
It gives you an idea of how your mountain's gonna look.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:53.870
And then we'll just blend the base of it out

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:55.990
'til it just floats there in the sky.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.490
You want it to just look like it's just

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:58.930
hanging up here in the mist.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.930
And now we can come back and begin putting in

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:05.730
all of our little highlights and stuff.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:09.430
And today, let's use, we'll use a small knife,

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:13.010
some dark sienna, dark sienna.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:16.370
I'm gonna be right back, I'm gonna get a little bright red

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.830
and put in there, maybe at least a little touch

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:23.020
of yellow ochre and pull it out very flat.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.080
Don't over mix it, leave it sort of marbled,

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.270
maybe even a little white here and there.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.000
See, that way you have all these

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.030
is happening, then cut across and you get that little roll

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.130
of paint, but all those various color mixtures are also

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:38.550
in that little roll of paint.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:43.810
Now then, no pressure, pressure.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:47.420
Just let the knife float right down the mountain.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:52.460
No pressure at all, see there?

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.580
Absolutely no pressure.

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:57.980
And we can take and just grab a little of that,

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:00.000
and all we're doing here is using a

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.000
a clean knife and sort of rubbing that a little.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.330
I wanna pull a little of that color down.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:07.270
We can add a little touch of blue here and there

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:15.830
to give it a little shadow effect.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:17.250
Drift right on down.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:21.050
Now then, with a large brush, I'm gonna tap that.

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:22.530
I wanna create mist 'cause I wanna push

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.590
that part of the mountain back.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.530
You can play little games when you're doing mountains.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:30.000
You can push parts of it way back into the distance.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.010
But the way you do that is with these misty areas

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:34.980
down here at the base.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:42.670
And then when we bring another layer over the top here,

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:48.380
we'll start right here, just let that slide right on down.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.920
When you bring this one down, directly in front,

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:57.190
it'll look like it's in the foreground.

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:59.080
See, and you get all these different colors

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.000
just sort of happening.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:03.720
just sort of happening here.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:07.090
And don't fight 'em, here we picked up quite a bit of white.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:13.860
Just sort of let these things happen.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.720
And then once again, I wanna mist this area.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:21.620
Just create that little soft, misty area.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:25.580
And with some of our dark color,

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:30.000
we can go back in here and create some heavy, dark shade.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.080
in there if we want to.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:37.780
Isn't that fantastic?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:42.010
It's a super easy, nice way to make some

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:44.880
very effective little mountains.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:46.960
I'll tell you what, let's do, let's get crazy.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:50.930
Maybe there's a little peak it lives right there.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:55.410
You know then, there.

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:58.960
You just sort of let it come right in front.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:10:59.860
Let's see how.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:02.290
and it pushes all that back.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:05.540
And you can do this and just create layer

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:07.000
after layer after layer of mountains.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.400
I was gonna have a small mountain here

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.620
and it just keeps growing, but that's alright.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:15.790
That's the way to learn.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.240
Make a lot of mountains, practice over and over.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.650
If there's a secret to this technique,

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:25.450
or to any technique of painting, it's practice.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:30.000
Devote some time to practice.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.640
I sincerely believe you can have anything

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.410
in this world that you want,

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:36.660
if you're willing to pay the price.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:40.220
And the price for this is practice, that's all.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.020
Anybody can do it, if you're willing

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.490
just to spend a little time practicing.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:48.540
And you'll be amazed at how quick it works for you.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:56.190
There.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:59.290
Now then, maybe today on this little mountain,

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:00.000
tell you what, maybe there's

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.500
some little grassy things that grow up here.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.970
I'll just use this little two-inch brush.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.890
Take a little sap green, a little yellow,

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:13.300
and just tap it, just tap, like so.

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:17.520
Now maybe, maybe there's some nice little grassy areas

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:20.830
that grow right up the side of this mountain.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:23.400
Look at that.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:24.980
Follow the angles in that mountain.

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:26.720
That's most, most important.

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:34.370
There we go, a little yellow ochre and Indian yellow

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:37.310
added here and there.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:40.460
This one here, we'll just let it drift right on off.

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.800
And you're picking up the mountain color

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.340
and just mixing with that so it all looks

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:49.080
like it flows together and it's all natural, looks right.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:57.970
Just let that grow and grow.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:04.230
And every once in a while, pick up a little dark color

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:07.290
and work that in too, so there's differences.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.730
There's light and there's dark.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:15.490
And you can always go back and add more little bumps

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:18.400
and rocks and stones, see there?

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:21.410
That easy, you can just continually add

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.290
all these little things, a little touch of highlight

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:24.900
here and there so it stands out.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.930
with the same colors.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:37.450
We can grab that, just the base of it,

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:40.400
and begin blending that out.

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:45.960
See, and from the other side, there it goes.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.950
And all of a sudden, that little projection,

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:51.170
he fits in there, he belongs.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:59.670
Everybody needs to belong somewhere, okay?

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:03.110
Make a little darker green here.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.870
Same colors, but a little darker green.

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:11.710
We'll sort of let that go up the back side here.

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:13.750
But you can just set a beautiful mountain

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:17.910
right out here in this little grassy area.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:18.920
Very much a problem.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.730
And the more you tap this, the softer it'll get.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:36.070
You can make it, I think I mentioned before,

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:39.600
you can make it to where it looks absolutely like velvet.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:44.240
Just a nice place to sit and look at

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:46.980
some of nature's masterpieces.

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:51.580
Hmm, I get carried away here sometime.

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:55.250
Now I tell you what, let's put some reflections under that.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:58.880
I'll go right into, we'll use a little black,

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.000
a little thing, a little blue.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:05.040
and just a couple of colors here on the brush, just tapping.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:08.830
Now then, decide where you want your reflections to be.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:11.080
And grab and pull straight down.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.010
It's important that you pull straight down.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:20.320
Just give it a little pull.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:21.940
Reflections used to drive me crazy,

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:26.420
and now they're one of the easiest things that we do.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:30.000
Because on this wet canvas, the paint will move.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.310
and you can make it as dark or as light as you want.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:44.240
Now very lightly, just go across.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.760
This will give it the shimmer, the glitter,

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.400
it looks like water.

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:53.720
And that easy, you have instant reflections.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:58.160
Go, isn't that fantastic?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.340
Now we take a little touch.

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.260
We'll use some Van Dyke brown.

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:08.700
Little tiny bit of dark sienna into it.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.220
Okay, cut off our little roll of paint again.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:13.600
That little roll of paint is so important.

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.560
It really will pay you great dividends

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:18.780
if you practice and learn to load the knife correctly.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:21.020
And just get in the habit of loading it

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:24.350
that same way each time.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.990
See, and that easy, you can just scrub in

00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:29.440
a little bit of land out here.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:36.870
All I'm doing is just sort of scrubbing.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:41.490
I think I'll put a big tree over there

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.940
so I don't have to worry about that.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:47.150
And a little bit of liquid white.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:50.640
You know me and my big trees, I like big trees.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:53.640
I'm gonna take a liquid white,

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:57.450
just lay in the indication of a little water line

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.000
under this land area.

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:06.120
like so.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:12.420
Act like you're trying to cut a hole in the canvas.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:20.540
And sometimes maybe you like to have a little,

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.360
just the indication of a little ripple here and there.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.770
All you do is just cut some across.

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.110
But all of them should remain basically straight.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:28.690
If they're not straight,

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.000
then they're gonna look like they're gonna run

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.420
right out of your painting, so.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:35.380
Tell you what, let's go into some of this dark color

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:41.030
we had left, pick up some Van Dyke Brown.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:44.280
We'll get a little sap greener, too, what the heck.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:47.300
Mainly dark colors, that's what you're looking for.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:50.340
And it's time to make some big decisions in your world.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:54.380
I tell you what, tell you what, maybe right here,

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:56.440
there's a land mass.

00:17:56.440 --> 00:18:00.000
So, we'll start off.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:04.040
There's some trees and shrubs and stuff that live out.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:06.380
There we go, there we go.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:07.590
See there?

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:09.280
Just sort of let these things happen.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:10.380
Just sort of look at your painting

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:12.400
and decide where you want a tree to live.

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:15.690
I think maybe a tree would be very happy

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:17.780
if he lived right out here.

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:22.770
That's a good place to put him.

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.620
Just sort of look around in your world

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:28.690
and decide where you think a tree would be happy.

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:29.600
Or a bush.

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:35.380
or house, just sort of look around.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:38.630
Yeah then, we'll have another tree right here.

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:40.960
We need to cover up that area.

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:42.920
It's important to me to leave a little bit

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:44.000
of this showing through,

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.680
so I wanna leave that showing through.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:50.470
That way you can see distance behind this.

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:57.390
Maybe this tree just, maybe he just comes right there.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:59.860
And underneath here, this will be reflections.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:04.510
and we're not committed yet.

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:06.310
We can make these reflections anywhere we want 'em,

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:08.860
just take a clean two-inch brush

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.210
and pull straight down,

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:12.810
wherever you decide reflections should be,

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:15.270
and go across.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:16.290
Isn't that easy?

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:20.160
Got instant reflections.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:22.370
Now then, we can take our,

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:23.630
we'll just use the fan brush today,

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:28.030
I'll take a little dark sienna and a little white,

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:29.190
just mix together.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:34.100
and let's just draw this through the tree.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.670
Then we'll make a little tree trunk.

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:38.490
Maybe we can only see a little bit of that one.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:40.570
It goes on off the canvas.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:43.710
Maybe this one has two in it, who knows?

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:46.580
You put as many or as few as you want.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.070
Now we need some nice leaves on there to brighten it up,

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:51.570
so I'll take the one-inch brush today.

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:56.020
You could do this with a two-inch brush or fan brush.

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:59.220
I'll tap it into some color, like so.

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:02.990
just tapping and sort of giving a little push, see?

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:06.000
Tap, give it a little push, okay?

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:08.230
Now then, let's go up here

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:11.650
and use just the corner of the brush

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:16.150
and just begin laying in some beautiful little leaf.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:19.270
Worry about shape and form here.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:21.530
I know you've heard me say that over and over,

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:24.670
but it's important, shape and form.

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:26.310
Don't just throw these on at random.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:34.100
yellow ochre, Indian yellow, cad yellow, sap green.

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:37.170
I like to just vary these colors over and over.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:39.440
There's a million different colors you can make.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:44.180
Okay, add a little, maybe a little touch

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:46.320
of the bright red to that.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:50.670
Get it to sparkle a little.

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:52.380
Put a little, a few little highlights

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:53.780
on this little sun we've got over here.

00:20:53.780 --> 00:21:00.000
Don't want it even left out.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:02.480
A little more of the green.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:04.620
And maybe down here on these bushes.

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:11.930
You can use this brush or whatever, whatever.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:18.750
Put all kinds of little things in.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:27.000
And just vary the colors.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.120
And you can reflect a little of this into the water.

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:36.830
like so, and take your large brush

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:39.960
and very lightly just graze it,

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:43.000
give it a little downward pull, and go across.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:45.880
And it gives the indication of some reflections in there,

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:48.220
just enough to make it nice.

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:52.230
We can go back to our Van Dyke Brown Dark Sienna mixture,

00:21:52.230 --> 00:21:55.490
and let's put in a happy little land area underneath here.

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:58.070
And same way as we did up here, we just scrub this in.

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:04.140
Just act like you're trying to rub it right through

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:07.220
wherever you want it.

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:10.310
A little bit of the liquid white.

00:22:10.310 --> 00:22:13.690
And with that, we can put in just a little water line

00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:20.030
underneath, there we go.

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:21.890
Take a clean knife and you can go back in here.

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:24.520
Normally in the dark areas in between these bushes,

00:22:24.520 --> 00:22:28.170
you can just put in the indication of little sticks

00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:30.000
and twigs and it helps create the

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.070
the illusion of depth in your painting.

00:22:32.070 --> 00:22:33.890
Distance between each bush.

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:37.150
We need something over here, let's get crazy.

00:22:37.150 --> 00:22:39.830
We'll use them same old colors we had.

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:44.540
Some sap green, some black, Van Dyke brown,

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:46.880
alizarin crimson, whatever you got.

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:49.110
Okay, let's go right up in here.

00:22:49.110 --> 00:22:53.640
Make a big decision, maybe, there it is.

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:59.190
We're gonna have a big something that's right here.

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:00.000
And all you have to do

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:05.380
is just start out and tap in a basic shape.

00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:08.210
Boy, that sound begins growing on me there.

00:23:08.210 --> 00:23:12.510
And that's all right, really the way to learn.

00:23:12.510 --> 00:23:14.790
Just throw 'em in, don't worry about 'em.

00:23:14.790 --> 00:23:17.850
And then make a painting out of it.

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:19.570
Used to, when I was teaching,

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:21.580
I would have students just take and sort of

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:24.650
turn their head away from the canvas

00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:27.310
and hit it with a big gob of color.

00:23:27.310 --> 00:23:30.000
And from that, their project for the day was to make

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:32.110
a beautiful painting.

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:35.860
That's one of the most fantastic ways I've ever found

00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:39.740
to learn just how to compose paintings

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:43.760
and to work with anything that happens.

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:46.930
Try that sometime, if you have an old canvas at home,

00:23:46.930 --> 00:23:49.470
just sock some color on it and go from that

00:23:49.470 --> 00:23:51.900
and turn it into a beautiful painting.

00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:55.470
You'll love what happens.

00:23:55.470 --> 00:23:59.730
Okay, go back to my fan brush we used to make the trunk.

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:02.920
And let's tell you what, let's have a trunk that lives

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:06.220
right there.

00:24:06.220 --> 00:24:08.360
Have to make those little noises or it don't work.

00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:11.520
Maybe this one's, he's got a crook in him.

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:15.730
Tired of seeing all of them just be perfectly straight.

00:24:15.730 --> 00:24:19.080
We can take paint thinner, a little Van Dyke brown,

00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:23.200
and here and there, add the indication of a few

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:25.760
little limbs that are living here.

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:29.860
See, wherever you want 'em, or as many or as few.

00:24:33.040 --> 00:24:34.860
See there?

00:24:34.860 --> 00:24:38.150
And if you have trouble making your paint flow,

00:24:38.150 --> 00:24:39.750
then it means your paint is just,

00:24:39.750 --> 00:24:41.580
it's not quite thin enough.

00:24:41.580 --> 00:24:42.780
Remember our golden rule,

00:24:42.780 --> 00:24:44.960
thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:46.970
I'm back to my one inch brush here.

00:24:46.970 --> 00:24:50.390
Just gonna tap some color into it, like so.

00:24:50.390 --> 00:24:54.330
A little bright red, a little yellow ochre, cad yellow.

00:24:54.330 --> 00:24:58.320
And let's go right up in here and,

00:25:00.190 --> 00:25:03.570
Put some nice little things that live out here on this tree.

00:25:03.570 --> 00:25:06.880
Once again, work with form and shape.

00:25:06.880 --> 00:25:11.260
Oh, I know you're tired of that.

00:25:11.260 --> 00:25:12.620
But if you're out here selling paintings,

00:25:12.620 --> 00:25:17.300
that's what brings that happy buck home.

00:25:17.300 --> 00:25:21.690
Individual shapes and forms.

00:25:21.690 --> 00:25:26.030
Here on this one, a few little things.

00:25:26.030 --> 00:25:27.450
Don't want him left out.

00:25:27.450 --> 00:25:29.440
Shoot, these time my guns will get mad

00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:32.340
Don't treat 'em all the same.

00:25:32.340 --> 00:25:34.550
They all want some beautiful little leaves

00:25:34.550 --> 00:25:41.840
and some bright sparkles on 'em.

00:25:41.840 --> 00:25:44.490
The other thing that will help in your painting,

00:25:44.490 --> 00:25:46.330
leave some dark areas underneath.

00:25:46.330 --> 00:25:48.480
There's usually a big shadow

00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:51.410
'cause all this stuff down here stops the light.

00:25:51.410 --> 00:25:55.310
So leave some shadows or some darker areas underneath.

00:25:55.310 --> 00:26:00.000
It'll help create that illusion of dark areas.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:03.200
we can begin, oh, maybe there's some happy little bushes

00:26:03.200 --> 00:26:07.200
that live right in here, wherever you want 'em.

00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:09.570
And you can just sort of drop these in.

00:26:09.570 --> 00:26:14.640
Ooh, there's a nice one, there's a nice one.

00:26:14.640 --> 00:26:22.640
Okay, like so, just wherever, wherever, and layer 'em.

00:26:22.640 --> 00:26:26.060
Put the ones as farthest away and work forward.

00:26:26.060 --> 00:26:30.000
That creates the illusion of distance.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.800
you can take a little brown and just lay it in, see?

00:26:32.800 --> 00:26:36.740
Make it look like there's a little dirt showing,

00:26:36.740 --> 00:26:41.880
and then put some happy little bushes all around that.

00:26:41.880 --> 00:26:44.960
Isn't that something?

00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:46.500
The old clock on the wall is telling me

00:26:46.500 --> 00:26:48.700
it's about time to go for today,

00:26:48.700 --> 00:26:50.500
but I really hope you enjoyed this painting.

00:26:50.500 --> 00:26:53.990
It'll teach you a great deal,

00:26:53.990 --> 00:26:58.010
make you become very comfortable with the equipment,

00:26:58.010 --> 00:27:00.000
and allow you to experience

00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:01.520
"The Joy of Painting."

00:27:01.520 --> 00:27:05.120
And from all of us here, happy painting and God bless.
